<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brandenburg an der Havel</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Brenna, Brennabor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> an der <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havel">Havel</a> is a city on the Havel in the German state of Brandenburg, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>. It began as Brenna, the chief stronghold of the Slavic Hevelli, where Otto I founded a bishopric in 948. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> secured it in 1157, and it gave its name to the March of Brandenburg and, ultimately, to the modern state. Its cathedral island preserves medieval buildings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brandenburg-an-der-havel.jpg" alt="Brandenburg an der Havel" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Queryzo derivative work:Regi51 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Johannis_in_Brandenburg_an_der_Havel_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
